/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 239 0 R
/T (browser-based database application that manages stock across multiple warehouses and controls every stock transfer through a defined life cycle. The system uses MySQL as the central database, Python \(Flask\) as the backend and HTML, CSS and JavaScript for the user interface \(technology choices for the frontend framework are stated as assumptions in this report\).)
/E (browser-based database application that manages stock across multiple warehouses and controls every stock transfer through a defined life cycle. The system uses MySQL as the central database, Python \(Flask\) as the backend and HTML, CSS and JavaScript for the user interface \(technology choices for the frontend framework are stated as assumptions in this report\).)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
341 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 239 0 R
/T (A transfer begins when a user creates a request from a source warehouse to a destination warehouse. The system validates that sufficient stock exists, and an authorised manager approves or rejects the request. After approval the goods are dispatched, and the stock is deducted from the source warehouse and shown as in transit. When the destination warehouse confirms receipt, the stock is added to the destination warehouse. All of these steps are recorded in transaction and audit tables, and database transactions guarantee that stock is never deducted without being added, or the reverse.)
/E (A transfer begins when a user creates a request from a source warehouse to a destination warehouse. The system validates that sufficient stock exists, and an authorised manager approves or rejects the request. After approval the goods are dispatched, and the stock is deducted from the source warehouse and shown as in transit. When the destination warehouse confirms receipt, the stock is added to the destination warehouse. All of these steps are recorded in transaction and audit tables, and database transactions guarantee that stock is never deducted without being added, or the reverse.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 239 0 R
/T (The database is designed up to the Third Normal Form, with primary keys, foreign keys and constraints that protect data integrity. Role-based access separates the powers of administrators, warehouse managers and inventory staff.)
/E (The database is designed up to the Third Normal Form, with primary keys, foreign keys and constraints that protect data integrity. Role-based access separates the powers of administrators, warehouse managers and inventory staff.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
